From 91897241b8896bd83992a3eb238bced6ba4f8087 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bob Van Valzah <Bob@vanvalzah.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 04:00:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Console: bare CR/LF no longer opens the interactive menu

Hardware-testing the external-control channel revealed that any byte -
including a stray line terminator - opened the interactive menu. A machine
client sending line-oriented $ commands with CR, LF, or CRLF endings would
have the trailing terminator drop the console into the menu, which then
echoed and consumed subsequent commands. Ignore bare CR/LF in updateSerial()
so the console is reliably scriptable; any other key still opens the menu.
---
 Firmware/GNSSDO_Firmware/menuMain.ino | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Firmware/GNSSDO_Firmware/menuMain.ino b/Firmware/GNSSDO_Firmware/menuMain.ino
index 0a360fa..a1b6cc6 100644
